{
  "summary": "Fixed parseInt radix parameter from 3 to 10. The bug: `parseInt('3', 3)` returns NaN because digit '3' doesn't exist in base-3 (only 0,1,2). This would have caused incorrect maxSessionsPerType values when env var was not set and no parameter was passed.",
  "learnings": [
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "Always use radix 10 with parseInt for decimal numbers unless specifically parsing non-decimal bases"
    },
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "Valid parseInt radix values are 2-36; digits must be less than the radix value"
    },
    {
      "topic": "parseInt radix",
      "reminder": "parseInt with invalid digit/radix returns NaN silently - always test edge cases"
    },
    {
      "topic": "TypeScript patterns",
      "reminder": "When parsing environment variables with parseInt, explicitly pass radix 10 to avoid subtle bugs"
    }
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "high",
      "type": "bug",
      "description": "The original code `parseInt('3', 3)` was broken - base-3 only has digits 0, 1, 2, so '3' is invalid and returns NaN",
      "location": "src/services/AgentSessionService.ts:24"
    },
    {
      "severity": "medium",
      "type": "test gap",
      "description": "No test verifies the constructor correctly parses NEZHA_MAX_SESSIONS environment variable with parseInt",
      "location": "src/tests/AgentSessionService.test.ts"
    }
  ],
  "suggestions": [
    "Add test for constructor behavior with environment variable parsing",
    "Consider using Number() instead of parseInt() for simple number conversion, or use parseInt(str, 10) consistently across codebase",
    "Add a comment explaining the radix parameter if there's any intention to support non-decimal bases in the future"
  ],
  "praise": "Bug caught and fixed. The change is minimal and targeted.",
  "overallScore": 85,
  "codeQualityScore": 90,
  "testCoverageScore": 75,
  "documentationScore": 80
}

